  "id": "social-facilitation",
  "term": "social facilitation",
  "definition": "Social facilitation is an increase in a motivated behavior that occurs when people do the same activity together, with mutual stimulation leading to greater coordination. It refers to improved performance or strengthening of the behavior in the presence of others engaged in it as well.",
